From b19f9d131b9189816e7242a019e8008c70a96f21 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Florian Stosse <florian.stosse@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 15:25:29 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] Don't negate INT64_MIN in QCBORDecode_ProcessBigNumber()

For a QCBOR_TYPE_INT64 item, QCBORDecode_ProcessBigNumber() computes
the magnitude with ABSOLUTE_VALUE(Item.val.int64) and with
-Item.val.int64, both in int64_t. For INT64_MIN, the CBOR negative
integer 3b 7f ff ff ff ff ff ff ff, the negation overflows, which is
undefined behavior (C11 6.5p5). It is reached from untrusted input,
e.g. the decimal fraction c4 82 00 3b 7f ff ff ff ff ff ff ff through
QCBORDecode_GetTDecimalFractionBigMantissa(), and by the existing test
case in qcbor_decode_tests.c, so UBSan flags the test suite.

Negate in uint64_t, which gives 2^63 for INT64_MIN, the value the
wrapping negation produced on common compilers.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/qcbor_number_decode.c | 9 ++++++---
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/qcbor_number_decode.c b/src/qcbor_number_decode.c
index e017ddb..37b8eda 100644
--- a/src/qcbor_number_decode.c
+++ b/src/qcbor_number_decode.c
@@ -1961,7 +1961,9 @@ QCBORDecode_ProcessBigNumber(const QCBORItem Item,
          break;
 
       case QCBOR_TYPE_INT64:
-         uLen = QCBORDecode_Private_CountNonZeroBytes((uint64_t)ABSOLUTE_VALUE(Item.val.int64));
+         /* Negate as unsigned: -INT64_MIN overflows int64_t */
+         uLen = QCBORDecode_Private_CountNonZeroBytes(bIsNegative ? 0 - (uint64_t)Item.val.int64 :
+                                                                    (uint64_t)Item.val.int64);
          break;
 
       case QCBOR_TYPE_UINT64:
@@ -2004,8 +2006,9 @@ QCBORDecode_ProcessBigNumber(const QCBORItem Item,
          break;
 
       case QCBOR_TYPE_INT64:
-         /* Offset of 1 for negative numbers already performed */
-         uIntTmp = (uint64_t)(bIsNegative ? -Item.val.int64 : Item.val.int64);
+         /* Offset of 1 for negative numbers already performed.
+          * Negate as unsigned: -INT64_MIN overflows int64_t. */
+         uIntTmp = bIsNegative ? 0 - (uint64_t)Item.val.int64 : (uint64_t)Item.val.int64;
          *pBigNumber = QCBORDecode_Private_UIntToBigNumber(uIntTmp, BigNumberBuf);
          break;
 
